# Build output. The image is identified by the SHA-256 in build-manifest.txt
# and in the evidence records; committing the binary would add a second copy
# that can drift from the sources that produced it.
build/

# Staged MCL sources. build.ps1 copies these from the canonical repositories
# at build time and records their hashes. Committing them would create a
# second copy of wire.c and link.c inside mcl-ap, which is exactly the drift
# the staging step exists to prevent -- and it would make "the board runs the
# same source the host runs" a claim rather than a fact.
dfr1154_mcl_node/src/
